.TH RUSTKET 1 "2026-11-08" "rustket" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustket \- native Rocket.Chat desktop client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustket
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fILINK\fR...]
.br
.B rustket
\fB\-\-dump\-policy\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustket
is a Rocket.Chat client that renders everything natively instead of embedding a
web browser. Browser sign-in (OAuth, OpenID, SAML, CAS) and video calls use the
default browser and return through \fBrocketchat://\fR links.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user: \fBrocketchat://\fR and
\fBhttps://go.rocket.chat/\fR links given on the command line are forwarded to
the running instance, which opens them; other arguments are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump\-policy " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Write the enterprise policy in effect (every source, value and problem found)
as JSON to \fIFILE\fR, or to standard output, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICED_BACKEND=tiny\-skia
Use the CPU renderer instead of the GPU (the same as turning hardware
acceleration off in the settings).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example \fBRUST_LOG=info,rustket=debug,rustket_core=debug\fR.
Logs are written to standard error. The default level never logs passwords,
tokens or message text; debug logs can contain message contents, room names and
user names, so review them before sharing.
.TP
.B RUST_BACKTRACE=1
Print a backtrace when the application crashes; include it in bug reports.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rustket/policies/managed/*.json
Enterprise policy set by the administrator. Files owned by root and not
writable by group or others, in a directory that is also owned by root and not
writable by group or others, are fully trusted. Other files are read with limited trust, which ignores
\fBManagedServers\fR and \fBSupportUrl\fR; see \fB\-\-dump\-policy\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustket/config.toml
Servers and preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/rustket/
Downloaded images (\fBimages/\fR, the oldest removed past the limit set in
Settings \(-> Storage) and media opened in another application (\fBmedia/\fR,
removed after 24 hours); decrypted end-to-end encrypted attachments are kept in
\fBmedia/e2e/\fR for up to 24 hours. Safe to delete while the application is
not running.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustket/<server id>/cache.sqlite
Offline cache of one server: rooms, settings, the newest messages and messages
written offline that were not sent yet. Deleted on logout or when the server is
removed; Settings \(-> Storage \(-> Offline cache \(-> Clear empties it but keeps
unsent messages. Do not delete it by hand while unsent messages may be queued.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustket/secrets.json
Fallback token store (mode 0600), used only when no Secret Service keyring is
available. Tokens are normally kept in the keyring.
